{
  "_comment": [
    "Oracle Database@Azure region and availability-zone catalogue. Feeds the",
    "location dropdown and the zone picker on the Azure page.",
    "",
    "Edit this file to add a region or zone - no code change needed. Restart the",
    "app to pick up changes.",
    "",
    "Source: docs.oracle.com/iaas/Content/database-at-azure/oaa_regions.htm",
    "",
    "Fields per entry:",
    "  region      Azure location name, e.g. 'eastus'. Unique; everything joins on it.",
    "  label       Human name shown in the dropdown, e.g. 'East US'.",
    "  zones       Availability zones where Database@Azure is offered, as the bare",
    "              numbers Azure uses. Single-zone regions list one entry.",
    "  group       Optgroup heading in the dropdown, e.g. 'North America'. Regions",
    "              are grouped in the order the groups first appear below.",
    "  status      'live' or 'planned'. Every Azure region here is live today;",
    "              the field exists so a planned region can be listed without",
    "              becoming selectable.",
    "",
    "zones_are_region_scoped is set because Azure numbers zones per region - '1'",
    "in eastus is unrelated to '1' in uksouth. It disables the cross-region zone",
    "uniqueness check that AWS and GCP rely on."
  ],
  "zones_are_region_scoped": true,
  "default_zones": ["1", "2", "3"],
